---
description: ASP.NET Core backend rules - clean layering, EF Core with PostgreSQL, contracts
globs: backend/**,shared/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Backend Rules

## Layers
- **Domain**: entities, enums, value rules. No references to EF Core, ASP.NET or other projects.
- **Application**: use cases/services and interfaces (e.g. repositories) per module in `Modules/<Feature>/`.
  Maps between Domain entities and `Mostawsef.Contracts` DTOs.
- **Infrastructure**: `AppDbContext`, `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` classes in `Persistence/Configurations/`,
  repository implementations, external services. Registered through `AddInfrastructure(connectionString)`.
- **Api**: thin controllers (`api/[controller]` or kebab-case `api/activity-logs`) that call Application services; no data
  access in controllers (except the `HealthController` database ping).
- **Contracts** (`shared/`): request/response DTOs (records). Allowed: DataAnnotations on request records and trivial
  computed helpers (e.g. `PageQuery.SafePageSize`). No business logic, no project or package references.

## Database
- Configure entities with Fluent API configuration classes (auto-applied by `ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly`), not attributes.
- Migrations live in `Infrastructure/Persistence/Migrations`; startup project is Api. The API applies pending migrations and
  seeds users (`Seed:Users`) on startup through `DatabaseInitializer`:
  `dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project backend/Mostawsef.Infrastructure --startup-project backend/Mostawsef.Api --output-dir Persistence/Migrations`
- Connection string key: `ConnectionStrings:Default` (dev value in `appsettings.Development.json`, Docker PostgreSQL).
- Portability (SQLite fallback): no PostgreSQL-only types/functions or raw SQL (not in migrations either: backfill
  existing rows with EF Core code from `DatabaseInitializer`); money as integer minor units. Only exception: index-only
  PostgreSQL features (the `pg_trgm` GIN indexes on log, order and patient `SearchText`), as long as the queries stay plain LINQ.

## Auth (see `Docs/auth.md`)
- JWT bearer auth is on. Every new controller/endpoint needs `[Authorize]` or a role policy
  (`AuthPolicies.AdminOnly`, `AuthPolicies.SuperOnly`); only `login` and `health` are anonymous.
- Passwords go through `IPasswordHasher` (PBKDF2). Never store, log or return a password or hash.
- Role names come from `Mostawsef.Contracts.Auth.Roles` / `Domain.Enums.UserRole`.
- Secrets (`Jwt:Key`) are never committed for production; dev values live in `appsettings.Development.json` only.

## Activity logs and system errors (see `Docs/logging.md`)
- Every main action in an Application service ends with `IActivityLogger.LogAsync(new ActivityEntry(...))`.
  Add its code to `ActivityActions` and an `Action.<code>` label to both desktop resx files.
- Unhandled exceptions are recorded automatically by `ExceptionHandlingMiddleware`: do not catch-and-swallow.
  If you catch and handle an exception, record it with `ISystemErrorLogger.LogAsync(ex, ...)`.
- Never log passwords, tokens or sensitive medical content in `Details`.

## Validation and errors (reference: the users module)
- Every error the client sees carries a stable code from `Contracts/Common/ErrorCodes` (the desktop translates
  `ErrorCode.<code>`): problem body `{ status, code, errors: { "Field": ["code"] } }`. Add new codes there and their
  text to both desktop resx files.
- **Shape** (required, length, format) = DataAnnotations on the request in Contracts with `ErrorMessage = ErrorCodes.X`
  (`Required`, `MaxLength` -> "max_length|50", `MinLength`, `Invalid`). Requests with validation use init properties, not
  positional record parameters, so the same attributes also run on the desktop. `[ApiController]` answers 400 automatically.
- **Business rules** (exists, unique, allowed state, own account) = Application service throws `AppException`:
  `Validation(field, code)` 400, `NotFound()` 404, `Conflict(code, field?)` 409. `ExceptionHandlingMiddleware` writes the
  problem response and does not record it as a system error. Controllers stay one-liners (no try/catch, no null checks).
  The older log endpoints return null/false for "not found"; new code uses `AppException`.
- **Invariants** (always true for the entity) = Domain constructor/methods (e.g. `User.NormalizeUsername`), plus database
  constraints (unique index, max length, required) in the Fluent configuration.
- Clamp, don't reject, harmless paging input (`PageQuery.SafePageSize`).
- No validation library (FluentValidation etc.) unless the user asks for one.

## Entities (Domain/Common)
- Business entities derive from `Entity` (Guid `Id`, `CreatedAt/By`, `UpdatedAt/By`, `Version`) or `SoftDeletableEntity`
  (+ `IsDeleted`, `DeletedAt/By`). `AuditInterceptor` fills these on every save; never set them by hand.
- `Version` is the concurrency token: edit requests carry the Version the client loaded; the service compares it and a
  race at save time also ends as 409 `concurrency_conflict`.
- Soft delete: `DbSet.Remove` marks the row deleted and a global filter hides deleted rows. `IgnoreQueryFilters()` only
  where deleted rows must count (e.g. a username is never reused).
- Writes that are not user edits (e.g. last sign-in time) use `ExecuteUpdateAsync`, so they don't change Version.
- Searchable names: store `SearchText.Normalize(value)` in its own column (e.g. `User.SearchName`), normalize the term the
  same way and compare with `Contains` (Arabic hamza/ta marbuta/alef maqsura, diacritics and Arabic digits handled).
  `SearchText` lives in `Contracts/Common` (the desktop filters local lists with it); Domain references nothing, so the
  Application service passes the normalized value into the entity (e.g. `PatientInput`, `new LabTest(code, name, searchName, ...)`).

## Time, numbers, money, reference lists
- **Clock**: inject `TimeProvider` (registered once in Infrastructure); never `DateTime.UtcNow`/`DateTime.Today` in
  Application or Infrastructure. Domain takes the time as a parameter when it matters. Tests swap it with
  `WithWebHostBuilder` + `ConfigureTestServices`.
- **Dates**: moments are UTC `DateTime` (`timestamptz`); calendar dates without a time (birth date) are `DateOnly` (`date`).
  "Today" is the server's local day (`LogPeriods.Current(time)`).
- **Readable numbers** (file no., invoice no.): `INumberSequence.NextAsync("patients")` + `DocumentNumber.Format("P", n)`
  -> `P-000123`. Safe across PCs; a failed save can leave a gap.
- **Money**: `long` minor units in entities, contracts and columns (`Contracts/Common/Money`: `ToMinor`/`ToMajor`, 100 per
  unit). The currency is `ClinicSettings.CurrencyCode` (one of `Currencies.All`); amounts never carry their own currency.
- **Reference lists**: fixed workflow values (order status, payment method) are C# enums stored as strings
  (`HasConversion<string>()`), sent as strings, and translated on the desktop (`{l:TrKey Status, Prefix=OrderStatus.}`).
  Lists the staff edit (lab tests, drugs) are real entities with their own module (copy the users module, `SearchName`
  for search). No generic lookup table.
- **Clinic settings** (`IClinicSettingsService`): name, address, phone, currency. One row, created at startup; everyone
  reads it, Admin edits it.
- **System settings** (`ISystemSettingsService`): backup folder and maintenance mode. One row, created at startup; Super
  only. While maintenance mode is on, `AuthService` refuses non-Super sign-ins with `409 maintenance_mode`.

## Conventions
- Async all the way with `CancellationToken` on I/O methods.
- Return proper status codes (400/401/403/404/409, 202/204 for no body); never leak exception details (the middleware returns a generic 500).
- Keep `GET /api/health` working: the desktop app relies on it (connection banner, version check). Increase
  `Contracts/Common/ApiVersion.Current` when a change removes or renames an endpoint or field the desktop uses.
